{"id":"frame-energy-db","t":"Frame energy in decibels","tags":["Data Processing","Time Series"],"d":"Easy","rt":"numpy","fn":"frame_energy_db","tol":[1e-06,1e-08],"pkgs":[],"st":"Write `frame_energy_db(x, frame_len, hop, eps=1e-10)` for a mono signal `x`.\n\n- Frame `i` covers samples `i*hop` to `i*hop + frame_len - 1`. Only full frames count, so there are $\\lfloor (N - L)/h \\rfloor + 1$ frames, or none if the signal is shorter than one frame.\n- The energy of a frame is the mean of its squared samples.\n- Return a list of $10\\log_{10}(\\text{energy} + \\varepsilon)$, one per frame.","starter":"import numpy as np\n\ndef frame_energy_db(x, frame_len, hop, eps=1e-10):\n    \"\"\"Mean-square energy of each full frame, in decibels.\"\"\"\n    x = np.asarray(x, float)\n    return [float(10 * np.log10(np.sum(x[i:i + frame_len] ** 2) + eps)) for i in range(0, len(x), hop)]\n","hints":["Build an index matrix of shape (n_frames, frame_len) and gather all frames at once.","Use the mean, not the sum, so the value does not depend on the frame length.","Decibels use 10 log10 for power (squared amplitude); 20 log10 is for amplitude."],"sol":"import numpy as np\n\ndef frame_energy_db(x, frame_len, hop, eps=1e-10):\n    x = np.asarray(x, float)\n    if len(x) < frame_len:\n        return []\n    n = (len(x) - frame_len) // hop + 1\n    idx = np.arange(frame_len)[None, :] + hop * np.arange(n)[:, None]\n    e = (x[idx] ** 2).mean(1)\n    return (10 * np.log10(e + eps)).tolist()\n","ex_md":"## Framing\nAudio is analysed in short overlapping frames, typically 25 ms long with a 10 ms hop. Short enough that speech is roughly steady inside a frame, long enough to hold a few pitch periods.\n\n## Why decibels\nLoudness perception is roughly logarithmic, and a speech signal spans a large dynamic range. On a dB scale, a fixed threshold like \"6 dB above the noise floor\" means the same thing for a quiet and a loud recording.\n\n## The epsilon\nDigital silence is exactly zero, and $\\log 0$ is $-\\infty$. The epsilon sets a floor (here $-100$ dB) so that silence becomes a very small finite number instead.\n\n## Interview follow-ups\n- Why does a pure energy detector fail on music, typing noise or a crowded café?","nex":2,"shown":[{"in":"[1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0]\n2\n2","out":"[4.3429451781522366e-10, 4.3429451781522366e-10]"},{"in":"[0.0, 0.0, 2.0, 2.0, 0.0]\n2\n1","out":"[-100.0, 3.0102999568569593, 6.020599913388197, 3.0102999568569593]"}],"lessons":[],"related":[],"ntests":5,"tj":"[{\"a\": [[1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0], 2, 2], \"e\": [4.3429451781522366e-10, 4.3429451781522366e-10]}, {\"a\": [[0.0, 0.0, 2.0, 2.0, 0.0], 2, 1], \"e\": [-100.0, 3.0102999568569593, 6.020599913388197, 3.0102999568569593]}, {\"a\": [[1.0, 2.0], 4, 1], \"e\": []}, {\"a\": [{\"__nd__\": [0.001257302210933933, -0.0013210486329130189, 0.006404226504432821, 0.001049001171530397, -0.005356693731611109, 0.0036159505490948474, 0.013040000451301373, 0.009470809631292421, -0.007037352358069926, -0.012654214710460526, -0.006232744625373522, 0.000413259793472436, -0.023250307746388345, -0.0021879166393254574, -0.012459109472530651, -0.007322673547034517, -0.005442589828573099, -0.0031630015636915456, 0.0041163053637413285, 0.010425133694426776, -0.0012853466294403427, 0.013664634705496859, -0.0066519467348661356, 0.0035151007009301973, 0.009034701816518087, 0.0009401229776087456, -0.007434992493538084, -0.009217253762584195, -0.004577258256673392, 0.002201951234700494, -0.01009618183538736, -0.0020917557487171307, -0.0015922500991447772, 0.005408455846858077, 0.002146591225063409, 0.003553727090399214, -0.0065382860941833945, -0.0012961363369276945, 0.007839754700613296, 0.014934311452207607, -0.012590655321041202, 0.015139237747390627, 0.013458754237823046, 0.007813114007004275, 0.0026445563032930354, -0.003139228145364278, 0.014580206835369588, 0.019602583164499646, 0.018016348698661252, 0.0131510376473437, 0.00357380410658956, -0.012083186322821715, -4.454133120083229e-05, 0.00656474935076335